{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:0.1", "PA_ya_5.3.2:0.2"], "en": "5. Saccayamaka 5.3 Pariññāvāra 5.3.2.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:0.3"], "en": "Atītavāra (The Chapter on the Past)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:1.1"], "en": "He who has fully understood the truth of suffering has abandoned the truth of the origin?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:2.1"], "en": "Yes. Or rather... [and so on]... Yes.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:3.1"], "en": "He who has not fully understood the truth of suffering has not abandoned the truth of the origin? Yes.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ya_5.3.2:4.1"], "en": "Or whoever... [as before] ...? Yes, it is so.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:29:40Z"}
